   "id": 1,
   "ref": "529–533",
   "en": "But not so the Phoenician queen, unhappy at heart: she is never released into sleep, or lets the night into her eyes or her heart. Her anxieties redouble, and her love, rising up again, rages and surges on a great swell of anger. So she persists, and thus turns things over within herself in her heart:",
