  {
   "id": 2,
   "ref": "534–539",
   "en": "'Well then, what am I to do? Am I, a laughing-stock, to try my old suitors again, and beg as a suppliant for marriage with the Numidians, men I have already refused so many times as husbands? Or should I follow the Trojan fleet instead, and obey the Trojans' every last order? Is it because they are glad to have been helped by my aid before, and gratitude for that old kindness stands firm among men who remember it so well?",
